# netsurf: grid fr sizing honours minmax floors; minmax(0, N) grows toward N (patch 337, with 337-libcss)
# Generated 2026-10-30
# Base: seleron/vitabrowser (patch stack through 336)
#
#  - layout_grid.c: a minmax(Npx, 1fr) track (fixes1214) was sized N PLUS
#    its fr share, so MDN's 240px sidebar took 469px of 960. CSS Grid
#    12.7.1: it is max(N, its share). A track whose floor exceeds its share
#    is fixed at the floor and the remainder re-shared, until none does.
#    The floors still stay reserved when auto tracks grow.
#  - New track kind 9 (minmax(0, Npx), css_rewrite "mxN"): base 0, grows
#    toward N with the free space left after fixed, auto and floor tracks,
#    before fr tracks share the rest (12.6 "maximize tracks" before 12.7).
#    MDN's article column is minmax(0, 48rem).
#  - css_rewrite.c: minmax(0, <px|rem|em>) emits "mxN" (it was folded to
#    1fr), and the emitter accepts the marker.
#
# repeat(auto-fill|auto-fit, minmax(N, 1fr)) uses the same track kind, so
# its columns are now max(N, share) rather than N + share. GRIDFILL206
# still passes 8/8.
#
# Gate: CSS-grid-fr-minmax (GRIDFR337 5/5, Chromium 5/5): minmax(100px,1fr)
# 1fr = 300/300 (was 400/200), minmax(400px,1fr) 1fr = 400/200 (was
# 500/100), minmax(0,300px) 1fr = 300/300, MDN's columns = 240/688 (was
# 469/229), minmax(15rem,1fr) 1fr. CSS-grid-named-var leg 3 now reads
# Chromium's 464.
